as you'll know spain under francisco  franco was neutral in the second world  war despite this it obviously had a  preference for the axis as well as  ideological sympathies towards the  regimes in italy and germany  given franco's preference this raises a  question after the fall of the axis why  didn't the allies get rid of franco as  well  so towards the end of the war franco  could tell which way the wind was  blowing and knew that the axis wasn't  going to win  as such he began to make friendly  overtures towards the allies  now he wasn't going to join the war on  the ally side or anything because one  spain was still recovering from the  civil war and two  germany was still in control of the  south of france until late 1944 and so  could have launched punitive actions  against spain  although after the fall of germany the  spanish government did consider  declaring war in japan to improve  relations with the allies  after the war was over and europe was  divided franco was pretty nervous about  his position  and with fairly good reason the ussr  demanded that franco be ousted first by  economic embargo and if that failed then  via military action  now the soviet union made these demands  because for them it was a win-win  if the allies removed franco then there  would be a fair shot that a communist  government could be installed in spain  and if franco stayed well then the west  wouldn't be able to criticize the ussr's  occupation and treatment of any eastern  european nations  since at that point it would be  hypocritical the western powers refused  to do this because they couldn't justify  another war to their people in a rough  country for fighting against a country  that hadn't really done much to oppose  them  so franco's main worry after the war was  france who disliked him for three  reasons  first he existed and openly coveted  french lands in africa  second france had recently been invaded  by a neighboring fascist country and it  really wanted to make sure that that  could never happen again  and third franco's government killed a  famous member of the french resistance  in late 1946 which outraged the french  public who demanded that franco be  removed by force  now franco had been busy for the past  few years making friends with the other  major western allies which he used to  his advantage he was particularly nice  to the british and had made arrangements  to hand over germans for trial to them  and also he promoted nonphalanges to  government to assure the british that  his regime could change  the americans didn't really buy it but  britain wanted a stable spain especially  one that wasn't going to invade  gibraltar  and thus britain made it clear that they  would oppose any french intervention  there  as such the french turned to the  americans to ask franco which they  agreed to do by forging a military coup  against him and replacing him with a  democratic government however britain  again refused to back this plan and  strongly argued against it  britain was concerned that spain would  enter into another second bloody civil  war and at the end of it there could be  a communist government in madrid  and in the end the americans decided not  to go ahead with it this was because  truman felt that western unity in the  face of communism was much more  important than removing franco and  in the end franco's gamble of simply  waiting paid off the allies soon turned  their attention to the east in combating  the spread of communism  something that franco could help with i  hope you enjoyed this episode and thank  you for watching with a special thanks  to my patrons  james bissonette kelly moneymaker  anthony beckett  the pastry section danny maloney rob  waterhouse  mo aaron the white james castaneda  jordan longley  jerry lamdin marcus asner gustav swan  john bailey  colin castleman rasheed ali spinning  three plates fielder oink oink izzy  david silverman maggie paxkowski winston  k wood  spencer lightfoot robert wetzel  fortunate calf lexi schwinn  sky chappelle and marvin cassell
 

